maj20|Judgement|Major Arcana|review, renewal, response|Look back with enough honesty to recognize a lesson and choose your next response. Growth involves answering what you now understand rather than endlessly rehearsing the past.|Self-condemnation and seeking a final verdict can prevent the practical work of repair.|Name one lesson from a past experience and turn it into a specific commitment.|What would responding differently look like this time?
maj21|The World|Major Arcana|completion, integration, perspective|Recognize a meaningful stage of completion and integrate what it taught you. Closing a cycle well can help you begin again with greater perspective.|Chasing a flawless ending can stop you from acknowledging genuine completion or unfinished details.|Review what is complete, settle one remaining detail, and acknowledge the effort involved.|What learning do I want to carry into the next chapter?
